http://edamontology.org/format_3747"},{"term":"uniprotkb-like format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2547"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"GPCR prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0472"},{"term":"MRM/SRM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3636"},{"term":"Protein feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3092"},{"term":"Topology diagram drawing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2486"},{"term":"Transmembrane protein visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2241"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein secondary structure image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1709"},"format":[{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"},{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]}]}],"name":"Protter","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ulo","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btt607","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: The ability to integrate and visualize experimental proteomic evidence in the context of rich protein feature annotations represents an unmet need of the proteomics community. Here we present Protter, a web-based tool that supports interactive protein data analysis and hypothesis generation by visualizing both annotated sequence features and experimental proteomic data in the context of protein topology. Protter supports numerous proteomic file formats and automatically integrates a variety of reference protein annotation sources, which can be readily extended via modular plug-ins. A built-in export function produces publication-quality customized protein illustrations, also for large datasets. Visualizations of surfaceome datasets show the specific utility of Protter for the integrated visual analysis of membrane proteins and peptide selection for targeted proteomics. \u00a9 2013 The Author 2013. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Ahrens C.H."},{"